            <ArticleTitle>[&quot;Off pump&quot; coronary surgery and simultaneous carotid endarterectomy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>67-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The occurrence of significant carotid artery disease in patients requiring coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG), results in a dilemma regarding the best surgical management. Our philosophy has been to perform simultaneous carotid endarterectomy and CABG off-pump. We reviewed the efficacy of this therapy in six patients treated in our hospital between January 2001 and December 2002. The result was satisfactory and there was no hospital mortality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
